    "problem": "Existing climate syntheses for the Eemian period are hampered by a lack of high-resolution data from high-latitude land areas, masking the crucial climate responses and feedbacks that occur in the Arctic during warmer-than-present conditions.",
    "method": "This study reconstructs high-latitude Eemian seasonal temperatures by applying an ensemble of pollen-climate calibration models to a high-resolution fossil record from northern Finland to address the scarcity of palaeoclimate data from the Arctic for this past warm period.",
    "task": "This paper's task is to reconstruct high-resolution Eemian seasonal temperatures from fossil pollen data in northern Finland to investigate decoupled seasonal trends and abrupt climate events in the Arctic under warmer-than-present conditions.",
